Complete Source Code Documentation
Overview of the Code Structure
The Terraform code is organized into modular components for better maintainability and reusability. Below is a breakdown of the key files and their roles:

1. main.tf
Purpose : Main configuration file that ties together all modules and resources.
Key Resources :
VPC Module : Sets up the network infrastructure.
IAM Role : Defines permissions for ECS tasks.
ECS Cluster : Creates the ECS cluster for hosting the worker.
ECS Task Definition : Specifies the container image, CPU/memory, and environment variables.
ECS Service : Deploys the worker as a service on Fargate.
2. variables.tf
Purpose : Defines input variables for customization.
Key Variables :
prefect_account_id: Your Prefect Cloud account ID.
prefect_workspace_id: Your Prefect Cloud workspace ID.
aws_region: AWS region where resources will be deployed.
prefect_api_secret_name: Name of the secret in AWS Secrets Manager.
3. outputs.tf
Purpose : Exports useful information after deployment.
Key Outputs :
ecs_cluster_arn: ARN of the ECS cluster.
worker_service_arn: ARN of the ECS service.
4. providers.tf
Purpose : Configures the AWS provider for Terraform.
Key Configuration :
Specifies the AWS region.
Ensures compatibility with Terraform v1.2.0 and above.
5. README.md
Purpose : Provides a user guide for setting up and deploying the infrastructure.
Sections :
Why Terraform was chosen.
Prerequisites (AWS CLI, Terraform CLI, Prefect Cloud account).
Step-by-step instructions for deployment.
Verification steps to confirm the setup.
6. report.md
Purpose : Summarizes the assignment approach, learnings, challenges, and suggestions for improvements.
Sections :
Tool choice: Terraform vs CloudFormation.
Key learnings from the project.
Challenges faced and how they were resolved.
Suggestions for future enhancements.
